# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots MariaDB and apache serving the vulnerable search.php
# (raw SQL string concatenation) and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the injectable endpoint is ALREADY live over HTTP when the agent starts,
#     so verify.sh probes the real SQL injection against a running stack;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting apache/mariadb cannot kill
#     the container.
#
# Note: mod_php re-reads search.php on every request, so patching it to use a
# prepared statement takes effect WITHOUT an apache restart - there is no
# "forgot to restart" variant. Preserving the CMD ensures the exploit is probed
# against a genuinely live service and a stopped/broken stack is a FAILURE.
